{"content":[{"c":["NETOPHAH, NETOPHATHITE"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Home and designation for two of David’s thirty mighty men (",{"href":"?bref=2Sam.23.28-29","r":"2Sam.23.28-29","rawR":"2Sam.23.28-29","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Sam.23.28-29","value":"2Sam.23.28-29"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Sm 23:28-29"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.11.30","r":"1Chr.11.30","rawR":"1Chr.11.30","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.11.30","value":"1Chr.11.30"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 11:30"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.27.13-15","r":"1Chr.27.13-15","rawR":"1Chr.27.13-15","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.27.13-15","value":"1Chr.27.13-15"}],"t":"ref","v":"27:13-15"},"). Seraiah, one of the captains who came to Gedaliah, the governor in Jerusalem after its fall to Babylon in 586 ",{"c":["BC"],"sourceClass":"era","t":"span"},", was a Netophathite (",{"href":"?bref=2Kgs.25.23","r":"2Kgs.25.23","rawR":"2Kgs.25.23","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Kgs.25.23","value":"2Kgs.25.23"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Kgs 25:23"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Jer.40.8","r":"Jer.40.8","rawR":"Jer.40.8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Jer.40.8","value":"Jer.40.8"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jer 40:8"},"). Fifty-six men of Netophah are mentioned as among the exiles who returned from Babylon with Zerubbabel and Joshua (",{"href":"?bref=Ezra.2.22","r":"Ezra.2.22","rawR":"Ezra.2.22","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezra.2.22","value":"Ezra.2.22"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ezr 2:22"},")."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"},{"c":[{"href":"?bref=1Chr.9.16","r":"1Chr.9.16","rawR":"1Chr.9.16","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.9.16","value":"1Chr.9.16"}],"t":"ref","v":"First Chronicles 9:16"}," speaks of Levites who lived in the villages of Netophathites, while ",{"href":"?bref=Neh.12.28","r":"Neh.12.28","rawR":"Neh.12.28","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.12.28","value":"Neh.12.28"}],"t":"ref","v":"Nehemiah 12:28"}," says that temple singers were gathered from the villages surrounding Jerusalem and from the villages of the Netophathites. Both of these references suggest that Netophah was the name of a district and not just of a town."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"},{"c":["The linking of Netophah with Bethlehem (see ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.2.54","r":"1Chr.2.54","rawR":"1Chr.2.54","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.2.54","value":"1Chr.2.54"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 2:54"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Neh.7.26","r":"Neh.7.26","rawR":"Neh.7.26","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.7.26","value":"Neh.7.26"}],"t":"ref","v":"Neh 7:26"},") indicates that it was in that vicinity. The actual site of Netophah is not known; however, the most probable location is the modern Khirbet Bedd Faluh, three miles (4.8 kilometers) southeast of Bethlehem."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"NetophahNetophathite","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"2 Sm 23:28-29","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Sam.23.28-29","rawQueryValue":"2Sam.23.28-29","sourceRefExact":"2Sam.23.28-29"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 11:30","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.11.30","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.11.30","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.11.30"},{"anchorText":"27:13-15","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.27.13-15","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.27.13-15","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.27.13-15"},{"anchorText":"2 Kgs 25:23","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Kgs.25.23","rawQueryValue":"2Kgs.25.23","sourceRefExact":"2Kgs.25.23"},{"anchorText":"Jer 40:8","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Jer.40.8","rawQueryValue":"Jer.40.8","sourceRefExact":"Jer.40.8"},{"anchorText":"Ezr 2:22","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ezra.2.22","rawQueryValue":"Ezra.2.22","sourceRefExact":"Ezra.2.22"},{"anchorText":"First Chronicles 9:16","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.9.16","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.9.16","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.9.16"},{"anchorText":"Nehemiah 12:28","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Neh.12.28","rawQueryValue":"Neh.12.28","sourceRefExact":"Neh.12.28"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 2:54","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.2.54","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.2.54","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.2.54"},{"anchorText":"Neh 7:26","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Neh.7.26","rawQueryValue":"Neh.7.26","sourceRefExact":"Neh.7.26"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"4bd1fab4faf4e1e7068acbf4eb6db87a0e013e1be5ba9ebde564b6fc22f5e194","sourceItemName":"NetophahNetophathite","sourceItemOrder":118,"sourceMember":"Articles/N.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"NetophahNetophathite","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Netophah, Netophathite","title":"Netophah, Netophathite","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}